        description {Returns the name assigned to the detected bot, browser or mobile application. The name is derived from the detected signature if detected, or the User-Agent string in combination with the detected anomalies.}
        source {https://clouddocs.f5.com/api/irules/BOTDEFENSE__bot_name.html}
        example {# EXAMPLE: Log the Bot name and Device ID of the client, upon each request, if it is known.
when BOTDEFENSE_ACTION {
    log local0.info "Bot [BOTDEFENSE::bot_name] with Device ID [ BOTDEFENSE::device_id] from IP [ IP::client_addr ] visited [HTTP::uri ]"
}}
        returns {The name assigned to the bot, browser or mobile application that sent the request.}
    }
}

