        description {Sets the status of the specified node or pool member as being down. If you specify no arguments, the status of the currently-selected node is modified.
Note: Calling LB::down in an iRule triggers an immediate monitor probe regardless of the monitor interval settings.

LB::down
    Sets the status of the currently-selected node as being down.

LB::down node <address>
    Sets the status of the specified node as being down.
    Doesn't work. Use LB::down or LB::down pool <pool> member <address> <port>. Refer to BZ222047 for details.}
        source {https://clouddocs.f5.com/api/irules/LB__down.html}
