        synopsis {POLICY::targets ('ltm-policy' |}
        description {Returns or sets properties of the policy rule targets for the policies
associated with the virtual server that the iRule is enabled on. A
policy rule target can be considered an action that the policy uses if
the rule conditions are met.

As of v11.4 the following policy targets are available:
 wam              - Application Acceleration Manager (AAM)
 asm              - Application Security Manager
 log              - Log
 http-cookie      - HTTP cookie
 http-header      - HTTP header
 http-host        - HTTP host header
 http-referer     - HTTP referer header}
        source {https://clouddocs.f5.com/api/irules/policy__targets.html}
        # TODO(spectcl): `hover` holds text no Tcl word carries verbatim — an
        #   unbalanced brace or a backslash-newline. A braced word is the only
        #   faithful spelling, so the statement is dropped rather than written
